  "result": "Perfect! All 297 tests pass. Foreign currency support is complete.\n\n**Implemented features:**\n\n1. **Currency rates constant** in `src/money.js`:\n   - `RATES = { EUR: 1, USD: 1.085, GBP: 0.8425 }`\n   - Units of that currency per euro\n\n2. **`convert(cents, currency)` function**:\n   - Converts euro cents to another currency\n   - Validates currency is supported (EUR, USD, GBP)\n   - Validates amount is non-negative integer\n   - Uses roundCents for precision\n   - Returns: `{ ok: true, value: cents_in_currency }` or `{ ok: false, error: \"UNKNOWN_CURRENCY\" }`\n\n3. **`formatMoney(cents, currency)` function**:\n   - Converts and formats amounts in any supported currency\n   - Currency symbols: \u20ac for EUR, $ for USD, \u00a3 for GBP\n   - Format: `$1,234.56` with thousands separators and 2 decimals\n   - Returns: `{ ok: true, value: formatted_string }` or error result\n\n4. **Error handling**:\n   - Added UNKNOWN_CURRENCY error code to src/errors.js\n   - Validates currency codes\n   - Validates amounts (non-negative integers)\n\n5. **20 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - RATES correctness and comparisons\n   - Identity conversion (EUR \u2192 EUR)\n   - Cross-currency conversions (EUR \u2192 USD/GBP)\n   - Large amounts ($13,395.05)\n   - Small amounts ($0.05)\n   - Zero amounts\n   - Rounding behavior (banker's rounding)\n   - Error cases (unknown currency, negative/non-integer amounts)\n   - Formatting with thousands separators\n   - Currency symbol correctness\n\nRequest 19 (Foreign Currency) complete. 297 tests pass.",
